ent_hash":"967f401e93b8f1e27796c2bf801c67b5536964c32523432080366d858494fa63","event_uuid":"a24d3e36-d1fa-473b-9385-9692f656232e","position":{"commit_sha":"9a7de4e2b94ff6e712e9165702d28b2c9290dc65","position":"1786141688370143001-a24d3e36-d1fa-473b-9385-9692f656232e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f13cfc3a4dbb92a8c1ed2c26586f31b5f4032f3115d356c3fc16e73e4a15b480","event_uuid":"a17f03cf-da91-48b6-8f9b-03c373281e1e","position":{"commit_sha":"e6d114c63dc37b7acfd6838fe27386382f923d93","position":"1786141773562579001-a17f03cf-da91-48b6-8f9b-03c373281e1e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1ee744e1f98506e172fa0bdc802331199db34f101810d231db28381c9fd14293","event_uuid":"70f52d1a-1766-468f-9cb6-f2c30a8de851","position":{"commit_sha":"e6d114c63dc37b7acfd6838fe27386382f923d93","position":"1786141774119271001-70f52d1a-1766-468f-9cb6-f2c30a8de851"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786140869666001001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b52128a5-15ee-4d97-80de-14e2624b3aff","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"baaf-d4f0-fa76-4450"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nThe `rebar-implement` skill (examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md) carries a \"Model\ntiering\" section that pins the implementer subagent to strong/standard/cheap model tiers to save\ntokens. This model-level gradient adds complexity (a tier table, per-dispatch tier-naming rules,\na dedicated 4e-bis \"Tier escalation\" ladder, per-leaf tiering session-log requirements) for\nsavings that only materialize on wide epics. We are removing it.\n\nSeparately, Phase 0's preflight hard-stops on any ticket with no children. That is too strict: a\n`story`/`task` with no children but a recorded file impact is already an executable code leaf —\nthe file impact is exactly the acceptance the completion-verifier close gate needs. The skill\nshould execute such a ticket as a single leaf instead of refusing it.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Remove the model-level gradient: delete the \"## Model tiering\" section; strip tiering language\n   from Phase 3 (non-code leaf), 4a, and 4d while PRESERVING the held-out discipline (the\n   implementer stays a separate subagent, which never depended on tiering); rewrite 4e-bis from\n   \"Tier escalation\" to a tier-free \"Escalation — when re-dispatch isn't enough\"; reground the\n   Phase 5 residual-sweep example.\n2. Allow a childless story/task with a recorded file impact to run as a single leaf: Phase 0\n   recognizes two executable shapes (has children -> tree; childless story/task with non-empty\n   `rebar get-file-impact` -> single leaf) and stops only when neither holds; add a Phase 2\n   callout collapsing Phases 3/5/6 to one change; update the frontmatter description, Phase 0\n   heading, and Reporting stop line.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] No \"Model tiering\" section and no strong/standard/cheap model-tier references remain in\n      SKILL.md. Proof: `! grep -niE 'model tiering|cheap.?tier|standard.?tier|strong.?tier' examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] The held-out separation (a separate implementer subagent) is still stated in Phase 4.\n      Proof: `grep -n 'separate' examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] Phase 0 documents executing a childless story/task with a recorded file impact as a single\n      code leaf, keyed on `rebar get-file-impact`. Proof:\n      `grep -n 'get-file-impact' examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md`\n- [ ] Frontmatter description, Phase 0 heading, Phase 2, and Reporting are consistent with both\n      changes (checked: manual read of the four sections).\n\n## Testing\n\nDocs-only change to a Markdown skill file; no source code changes, so the CI `Verified` gate\n(`make lint && make typecheck && make test`) is unaffected and passes unchanged. Verify the\nacceptance criteria with the grep commands listed above, run from the worktree root.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md","reason":"Remove Model tiering section and refs; add single-leaf path"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","baaf-d4f0-fa76-4450"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a17f03cf-da91-48b6-8f9b-03c373281e1e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2b4f-b0ca-e5d8-4c3f","ticket_type":"task","title":"rebar-implement: remove model-tiering gradient; run a childless story/task with file impact as a single leaf","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["11fd934d-80ad-422d-aba2-2e08de76630a","74126403-69a6-4359-83cf-58d59f11f678","26c8d9bc-f995-4f45-bd59-1a25bb02e2e8","4e91e3ab-dc0c-4f7b-a6a6-352a22900e1a","a24d3e36-d1fa-473b-9385-9692f656232e","a17f03cf-da91-48b6-8f9b-03c373281e1e","70f52d1a-1766-468f-9cb6-f2c30a8de851","b52128a5-15ee-4d97-80de-14e2624b3aff"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786142051960899134,"uuid":"66d9cc5a-3156-441b-a157-06c29bc56a08"}